From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] zfs.kext doesn't start with less than 1 GB of memory

The SPL's vmem setup (spl-vmem.c) VERIFYs at least 1 GB of memory, so
on a smaller machine zfs.kext's start() panicked the kernel: "VERIFY3U(
real_total_memory >= 1024ULL*1024ULL*1024ULL) failed (536870912 >=
1073741824)". macOS machines never have less; NeoDarwin's QEMU tests run
at 512 MB, and since P3-11 checkpoint 5 the kext is in every boot. start()
now declines below 1 GB with a console line, before the SPL starts, and
the kernel boots without ZFS (a ZFS root then can't be mounted, which
upstream never supported at that size either).

Rebase-risk: low
---
diff --git a/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/zfs_osx.cpp b/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/zfs_osx.cpp
--- a/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/zfs_osx.cpp
+++ b/module/os/neodarwin/zfs/zfs_osx.cpp
@@ -187,6 +187,25 @@
 	if (!res)
 		return (res);
 
+#ifdef __NEODARWIN__
+	/*
+	 * The SPL's vmem setup VERIFYs at least 1 GB of memory and panics
+	 * below it. zfs.kext is in every boot (P3-11 checkpoint 5), and
+	 * machines with less (QEMU tests with 512 MB) must boot without it.
+	 */
+	{
+		uint64_t memsize = 0;
+		size_t len = sizeof (memsize);
+		(void) sysctlbyname("hw.memsize", &memsize, &len, NULL, 0);
+		if (memsize != 0 && memsize < (1ULL << 30)) {
+			IOLog("ZFS: not starting: %llu MB of memory; ZFS "
+			    "needs 1024 MB\n", memsize >> 20);
+			super::stop(provider);
+			return (false);
+		}
+	}
+#endif
+
 	/* Fire up all SPL modules and threads */
 	spl_start(NULL, NULL);
 
